# Docker build-context exclusions (06-03-PLAN.md Task 1). Load-bearing for two things:
# 1. Keeping a real `.env` (live secrets) out of every published image layer -- `.env` and
#    `.env.*` are excluded with NO negation here, unlike .gitignore's `!.env.example`. A build
#    context is a much larger blast radius than a git commit: a real .env sitting next to this
#    file would be silently baked into a publicly-pushed image layer forever (T-06-18).
# 2. Keeping host `node_modules` (platform-specific native builds of argon2/ssh2) from shadowing
#    the image's own `pnpm install` output -- every stage in apps/control-plane/Dockerfile and
#    apps/web/Dockerfile installs its own node_modules against the image's own architecture.
#
# Do NOT exclude pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, turbo.json, package.json, apps/**,
# packages/** source, or install.sh -- the Dockerfiles' pruner/installer/builder stages need all
# of these to reproduce a real `turbo prune --docker` + `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` build.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.turbo
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.env
.env.*
.planning
.claude
docs
tests
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
